  <metadata>
    <name>Lewotobi southern corridor via Boru</name>
    <desc>Lewotobi southern corridor via Boru (alternative): South of the Lewotobi twins through Boru on and around the Trans-Flores corridor. Only usable if the volcano's alert level and exclusion radius allow it on race day; the north-coast line stays the primary. 117.6 km, +1812 m. Replaces 95.6 km / +1246 m of the main course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:59Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.545100" lon="122.517400">
    <ele>3.6</ele>
    <name>Talibura</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: none | position approximate -- Easternmost and largest kecamatan of Sikka Regency, on the Flores Sea coast approaching the Flores Timur border; has a mangrove coast (Desa Darat Pantai). Two Wikidata entries for 'Talibura' disagree by several km and bo</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.526390" lon="122.711390">
    <ele>274.0</ele>
    <name>Boru</name>
    <desc>km 49.1 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- Wulanggitang kecamatan capital on the Trans-Flores highway between Maumere and Larantuka; a handful of roadside restaurants and the PVMBG Lewotobi volcano observation post are nearby. Relevant only to Alternative B (the </desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347500" lon="122.979700">
    <ele>13.0</ele>
    <name>Larantuka</name>
    <desc>km 117.6 | kind: finish | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Race finish town: capital of Flores Timur Regency, historic Portuguese-Catholic port under Ile Mandiri, host of the Semana Santa Holy Week procession. Also a port (ferries to Adonara, Solor, Lembata, Kupang) and near Gew</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Red</sym>
    <type>anchor/finish</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.314800" lon="122.968000">
    <ele>1469.4</ele>
    <name>Ile Mandiri</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike] Dormant volcano (commonly cited 1,502 m, DEM peak ~1,469 m) rising directly behind Larantuka; the mountain the finish town sits under, and the subject of a proposed optional final hike-a-bike 'sting in the tail'.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.346500" lon="122.980000">
    <ele>21.6</ele>
    <name>Kapela Tuan Ma</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] Small waterfront chapel housing the venerated Tuan Ma (Our Lady) statue, the focal point of Larantuka's Semana Santa: on Good Friday the statue is carried in procession to Kapela Tuan Ana and back through the town.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347000" lon="122.979700">
    <ele>16.4</ele>
    <name>Reinha Rosari Cathedral</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] Seat of the Roman Catholic Diocese of Larantuka, dedicated to Mary Queen of the Rosary; the cathedral around which the Semana Santa Holy Week processions are organised each year.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347500" lon="122.979700">
    <ele>13.0</ele>
    <name>Larantuka -- Semana Santa and Portuguese Heritage</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Portuguese-Catholic port town at Flores' eastern tip, seat of the historic Kingdom of Larantuka and host of Semana Santa, a Holy Week procession tradition local sources describe as unbroken since the 16th century; the race's Portuguese-heritage bookend to Sikka in the west.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.538600" lon="122.767000">
    <ele>1569.6</ele>
    <name>Lewotobi Laki-laki</name>
    <desc>[hazard, hike-a-bike] The more active of Flores Timur's twin volcanoes (1,584 m); erupting repeatedly since Nov 2024 with fatalities and a standing PVMBG exclusion radius. Treated as a no-go zone for course planning; see hazard_level.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
